invariant: INV-17
file: src/widemul_p256.h
catches: p256_adx_model_test
reason: widemul_p256_point_mul no longer calls p256_wide_wipe_below after
  the call into the x86-64 field's copy. Every object that call names is
  still wiped, so the vectors pass: what stays is whatever the compiler
  spilled of the scalar and every multiple of the point the ladder held,
  in the frames under the dispatcher's caller. bin/p256_adx_model_test
  runs the dispatch over the model on every host, calls each dispatcher
  over a painted stack and requires zero where the wipe's array lay.

--- old
        p256_adx_mul(o, k, p);
        p256_wide_wipe_below();
--- new
        p256_adx_mul(o, k, p);
